{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-13939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/assets/555cdb44522fab12ad67b54042ee4e47a085802df65c2b32a512eace16b92dd4.png)\n\nCalculate the area of the parallelogram in the figure." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-13939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we get the vectors\n\n$$\n\\text{u}=⟨1,2⟩,\\,\\text{v}=⟨2,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|-5\\,|=5\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-13939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "71a94be75fc9bf89f92e07f1bcc70a5c4dc33378bc2c8d6da1b46c650a6c7dae"} {"question" "q-13939" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-13939" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-13939" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 0-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "71a94be75fc9bf89f92e07f1bcc70a5c4dc33378bc2c8d6da1b46c650a6c7dae"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}+3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-69941" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-102760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-102760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1-(-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =3-3 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-102760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "71a94be75fc9bf89f92e07f1bcc70a5c4dc33378bc2c8d6da1b46c650a6c7dae"} {"question" "q-102760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-102760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-102760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/assets/f63cf622acc15681e3815118bbd2a187ea6039a548d4be1773634c0dc450c343.png)\n\nDetermine the area $A$ of the parallelogram in the figure.\n\n$\\,\\,A=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we get the vectors\n\n$$\n\\text{u}=⟨4,-1⟩,\\,\\text{v}=⟨-2,-3⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-3)-(-2)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-12-2 \\\\  & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|-14|=14\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "71a94be75fc9bf89f92e07f1bcc70a5c4dc33378bc2c8d6da1b46c650a6c7dae"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-320394" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-320550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=⟨\\frac{3}{2},-5⟩$ and $\\text{v}=⟨a,6⟩$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-320550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} & a \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} & a \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 6-a\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =9+5a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9+5a & =0 \\\\ 5a & =-9 \\\\ a & =-\\frac{9}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-320550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "71a94be75fc9bf89f92e07f1bcc70a5c4dc33378bc2c8d6da1b46c650a6c7dae"} {"question" "q-320550" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"} {"question" "q-320550" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{9}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972686/state.json" "file_sha256" "3160b576cc2ebd985a377b4154428d331b8f83d432fdcbc0c2efa8382e588160"}] "usage" {} "basis" 664 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
